<p>You know, I’ll say this isn’t the most intriguing anomaly, that it’s a bit long for the amount of provided intrigue, and the whole “ghost that roams these caves” bit is a tad cliche, but the article is engaging in its prose to me (I wanted to finish it), it gives us a really layered support for the cliche, is based on some real-life stuff, and I found myself thinking about this article fondly several days after I read it.</p>
<p>So all that indicates to me this is worthy of a +1, even if there are some intangibles as to my reasoning why.</p>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> I have a real fear of spelunking and falling down crevices in caves. Maybe that’s all that’s going on on my end here. But I feel like there’s more.</p>
<p>Also, I would’ve normally kept track of things like this to change them for you, but I know there were some syntactical and grammatical errors in this. Not many.</p>

